window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-008", "name_zh": "内在自我", "name_en": "inner ego", "tagline": "赛斯说你不只有眼前这个「我」：还有一个同样清醒、一直在幕后指挥身体、组织事件、连接内在实相的内在自我——所谓无意识，其实是另一个更有意识的你。", "explanation": "内在自我（inner ego，或称内我、内在自我意识）是赛斯人格结构论的核心角色：你有一个人人熟知的、导向物质世界的外在自我，也有一个同样完全清醒、导向内在实相的内在自我。心理学家所谓的「阈下自己」或「无意识」，在赛斯看来其实是另一个更有意识的存在——它的推理不输已知的自我，还更有弹性和知识。它是你真正的操作者：从里面指挥身体与所有存活机制，透过精神基因系统把能量转成分子、把能量单位转成物质，在架构二里安排事件的成形——包括你的工作机遇与不知不觉的痊愈。外在自我只是它的前台假象，双方各管一区、互为张力：内我向发端的冲动冲刺，外我向外操控物质。两者的重新连接走梦的路：内在自我就是做梦的自己，梦境处理两个架构的事件并把它们转译成象征；当两个自我在梦里或醒时融合，直觉泉源会涌到表面，那代表一种新意识的形成。它活在广阔的现在里，看见本体同时存在于各维度，也是肉体死后存活的那个「我」——但它并不比你优越，而是你人格中具有最高抱负与能力、并自视为宇宙所挚爱的个别化部分。", "definitions": [{"zh": "我称这似是无意识的部分为“内在自我”，因为它指挥内在的活动。它把非由肉体感官却经由其他内在管道得来的资料联系起来。它是实相的内在感知者，而它的存在超越了三次元之外。", "en": "I call this seemingly unconscious the “inner ego,” for it directs inner activities. It correlates information that is perceived not through the physical senses, but through other inner channels. It is the inner perceiver of reality that exists beyond the three-dimensional.", "source": "Session 512"}, {"zh": "就如你有一个完全有意识的，被导向物质世界的“自我”，你也有一个导向内在实相的“内在自我”。换言之，你有一部分完全有意识的自己是在“架构二”里。", "en": "As you have an ego, fully conscious, directed toward the physical world, you also have what I call an inner ego, directed toward inner reality. You have, in other words, a portion of yourself that is fully conscious in Framework 2.", "source": "Session 822"}, {"zh": "内在自我是全然有意识的。", "en": "The inner ego is fully conscious.", "source": "Session 822"}, {"zh": "我过去所谓的内心自我向来都会考虑到人格的整体需求。现在，这部分的自己确实是有着最高层意义的自我意识——对人格的潜意识部分是有觉知的，对你称之为自我的主要意识架构是有觉知的，而且持续不断指挥全部的活动。这个部分对神经系统和所有身体功能的复杂运作是有觉知的。 它是监督者。它知道允许潜意识的需求和愿望得以实现，它知道何时停顿实现。负责整体稳定的正是人格的这个部分", "en": "The overall needs of the personality are always taken into consideration by what I have called in the past the inner ego. Now this portion of the self is indeed self-conscious in the highest meaning of the term—aware of the subconscious portion of the personality, aware of the primary conscious framework that you call your ego, and constantly directs the overall activities. This portion is aware of the complicated workings of the nervous system and all bodily functions. It is the overseer. It knows when to allow subconscious needs and wishes their fulfillment. It knows when to put fulfillment off for a time. It is this part of the personality that is in charge of overall stability.", "source": "Session 270"}, {"zh": "现在。这个内在自我也可以在梦状态中运作，而且在某些看似醒着的梦中，发觉人格不在它平常的醒时状态也正是它。在最佳的投射中与你同在的，正是自己的这个部分。内在自我是人格当中具有最高的抱负和能力的那个部分。心理学家称之为阈下的自己（subliminal self）。", "en": "Now. This inner ego can also operate within the dream state, and in certain awake-seeming dreams it is the portion that realizes that the personality is not in its normal waking condition. It is this portion of the self that is with you in the most excellent projections. The inner ego is the part of the personality that contains the highest aspirations and capabilities. It has been called by psychologists the subliminal self.", "source": "Session 270"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "它是什么：另一个完全清醒的你", "note": "AI总结：赛斯给它的名字不止一个——内在自我、内我、内在自我意识——但核心意思一致：在每个人格之中都有这样一个部分，它知道自己的源头，是那个「呼吸者」和「做梦者」背后真正的操作者。它不是模糊的本能：赛斯明说它是全然有意识的，是具有最高层意义的自我意识——对潜意识部分有觉知，对人称「自我」的主要意识架构有觉知，还持续指挥全部活动；心理学家叫它「阈下的自己」，它包含人格里最高的抱负与能力。《灵魂永生》里的定义最完整：他称之为内在自我的，是那个似是无意识的部分，因为它指挥内在活动，把不经肉体感官、而经内在管道得来的资料联系起来，是超越三次元之外的实相内在感知者。在《个人与群体事件的本质》里它被放进架构二的语境：你有一个导向外在物质世界的自我，也有一个导向内在实相的内在自我——你有一部分完全有意识的自己就住在架构二里；所谓「无意识」其实有意识，它的推理不是无理性的，方法也不混乱，其特性不输已知的自我，还更有弹性、更有知识。它连结两个世界：一边是纯心灵的存有实相，一边是主要物质的自己。但别把它神化成高你一等的主子——它不该被认为比你的凡心优越，也不是与凡心分开的东西；它自视为宇宙一个被挚爱的、个别化的部分，对那份与生俱来的宇宙大爱有觉察。", "src": "第 3、28、35、202、270、512、822、823、894 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 3 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 28 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 35 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 202 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 270 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 822 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 823 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 894 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-008-e0001", "zh": "存有本身不必持续不断追踪他的人格，因为在每一个人格之中都有一个内在自我意识（inner self-conscious）的部分，知道它的源头。现在，我称这个部分为超越潜意识的自我意识。那个呼吸者、以及那个做梦者，似乎并非像看起来那样被自动控制。此前我已经说过，你的某些部分完全知道肺呼吸了多少氧、在地板上踱步需要多少能量，而这就是我说的那个部分的你。就是这个部分，以及自我意识的部分，接收所有的内在资料。", "en": "The entity itself does not have to keep constant check on its personalities, because in each personality there is an inner self-conscious part that knows its origin. This part, for now, I will call the self-conscious beyond the subconscious. The breather and the dreamer are not so automatically controlled as it would seem. I have mentioned before that some part of you knows exactly how much oxygen the lungs breathe, and how much energy it takes to pace a floor, and this is the part of you of which I spoke. It is the part, and the self-conscious part, that receives all inner data.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第28节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "28", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0002", "zh": "内在自我或内在自我意识自己指挥着这样的经验，并以使用内在感官，方式和你们使用外在感官差不多，但内在自我认识使用内在感官涉及的所有机制，而你们对外在感官涉及的机制却认识很少。", "en": "The inner ego or the inner self-conscious self directs such experiences and uses the inner senses in much the same way that you use the outer senses, except that the inner ego knows all of the mechanics involved in the use of the inner senses, and you know little of the mechanics involved with the outer senses.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0090", "zh": "内在自我就是内在本体。它很靠近存有，连结着一个纯心灵的、存有的实相，和一个主要物质的、物质自己的实相。", "en": "The inner ego is then this inner identity. It is closely allied with the entity, and connects a reality that is purely psychic, the reality of the entity, with a reality that is mainly physical, the reality of the physical self.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第202节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "202", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0100", "zh": "我过去所谓的内心自我向来都会考虑到人格的整体需求。现在，这部分的自己确实是有着最高层意义的自我意识——对人格的潜意识部分是有觉知的，对你称之为自我的主要意识架构是有觉知的，而且持续不断指挥全部的活动。这个部分对神经系统和所有身体功能的复杂运作是有觉知的。 它是监督者。它知道允许潜意识的需求和愿望得以实现，它知道何时停顿实现。负责整体稳定的正是人格的这个部分", "en": "The overall needs of the personality are always taken into consideration by what I have called in the past the inner ego. Now this portion of the self is indeed self-conscious in the highest meaning of the term—aware of the subconscious portion of the personality, aware of the primary conscious framework that you call your ego, and constantly directs the overall activities. This portion is aware of the complicated workings of the nervous system and all bodily functions. It is the overseer. It knows when to allow subconscious needs and wishes their fulfillment. It knows when to put fulfillment off for a time. It is this part of the personality that is in charge of overall stability.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第270节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "270", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0101", "zh": "现在。这个内在自我也可以在梦状态中运作，而且在某些看似醒着的梦中，发觉人格不在它平常的醒时状态也正是它。在最佳的投射中与你同在的，正是自己的这个部分。内在自我是人格当中具有最高的抱负和能力的那个部分。心理学家称之为阈下的自己（subliminal self）。", "en": "Now. This inner ego can also operate within the dream state, and in certain awake-seeming dreams it is the portion that realizes that the personality is not in its normal waking condition. It is this portion of the self that is with you in the most excellent projections. The inner ego is the part of the personality that contains the highest aspirations and capabilities. It has been called by psychologists the subliminal self.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第270节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "270", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0127", "zh": "我称这似是无意识的部分为“内在自我”，因为它指挥内在的活动。它把非由肉体感官却经由其他内在管道得来的资料联系起来。它是实相的内在感知者，而它的存在超越了三次元之外。它携带着你们每个前生的记忆。它探入实际上是无止境的主观次元，所有客观的实相都是由这些主观次元源源流出的。（停了很久）", "en": "I call this seemingly unconscious the “inner ego,” for it directs inner activities. It correlates information that is perceived not through the physical senses, but through other inner channels. It is the inner perceiver of reality that exists beyond the three-dimensional. It carries within it the memory of each of your past existences. It looks into subjective dimensions that are literally infinite, and from these subjective dimensions all objective realities flow. (Long pause.)", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0132", "zh": "就如你有一个完全有意识的，被导向物质世界的“自我”，你也有一个导向内在实相的“内在自我”。换言之，你有一部分完全有意识的自己是在“架构二”里。在你们普通世界——我们仍称之为“架构一”——里的自我是特为配备好去处理那个环境的，它以因与果及顺序性时刻来操纵，它处理一个客观化的实相。它可以延展它的能力，而变得比平常更觉察内在事件，但其主要目的是与“果的世界”打交道，去接触事件。", "en": "As you have an ego, fully conscious, directed toward the physical world, you also have what I call an inner ego, directed toward inner reality. You have, in other words, a portion of yourself that is fully conscious in Framework 2. The ego in your ordinary world, which again we will call Framework 1, is uniquely equipped to deal with that environment. It manipulates with rules of cause and effect and consecutive moments. It deals with an objectified reality. It can stretch its capacities, becoming far more aware of inner events than it is normally allowed to do, but its main purpose is to deal with the world of effects, to encounter events.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0133", "zh": "内在自我是全然有意识的。不过，它是你的一个部分，负责处理事件的形成，而得意的沉浸在被你们特定的时空所具体排除的一个颇具韧性与创造性的活动里。所谓的无意识，是——我以前说过——相当有意识的，却是在另外的活动领域里。可是，在“自己”这两个部分之间必然有一个心理小室——这些仿佛未区分的地区，在其间发生往复的转译。当然，做梦时间提供了那种服务，因此，在梦里这两个自我能会面，而融合到某个范围，就像在一辆夜车上可能碰头的陌生人在交换意见，而在谈了一会儿之后，惊奇的发现它们真的是很近的亲戚，它们二者都在这同样的旅程上，虽然它们看似单独在旅行。", "en": "The inner ego is fully conscious. It is a portion of you, however, that deals with the formation of events, that glories in a rather rambunctious and creative activity that your specifications of time and place physically preclude. The unconscious, so-called, is — and I have said this before2 — quite conscious, but in another realm of activity. There must be a psychological chamber between these two portions of the self, however — these seemingly undifferentiated areas, in which back-and-forth translations can occur. Dream periods provide that service, of course, so that in dreams the two egos can meet and merge to some extent, comparing notes like strangers who perhaps meet on a train at night, and are amazed to discover, after some conversation, that they are indeed close relatives, each embarked upon the same journey though seemingly they travelled alone.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0141", "zh": "我大半是在对西方的听众说话，因而，在此我是为了这个特定的理由来选用名词，以便以一种能被了解的方式来解释观念。作为一个适合我的目的之名词，“内我”是很完美的。让我再度强调“无意识”的确是有意识的——当我说它有意识，我是指它的推理并不是无理性的，它的方法并不是混乱的，而它的特性不但相等于那已知的自我的特性，还更加具有弹性及知识呢！", "en": "I am speaking largely to a Western audience, and so here I am using terms for a particular reason, to explain concepts in a way that will be understood. The inner ego (see the last session) is perfect as a term to suit my purposes. Let me stress again that the “unconscious” is indeed conscious — and by conscious I mean that its reasoning is not irrational. Its methods are not chaotic, and its characteristics are not only equal to those of the known ego, but indeed are more resilient and knowledgeable.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第823节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "823", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0149", "zh": "那么，你是一个自己，但为了操作的目的，我们将说你有三个部分：内我或内在自我，身体意识，以及你所知的意识。", "en": "You are one self, then, but for operating purposes we will say that you have three parts: the inner self or inner ego, the body consciousness, and the consciousness that you know.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第894节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "894", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0151", "zh": "真的是不可能分开自己各部分的，而我们做这种区分，只是想解释人格（personality）之许多面向（facets）的一个努力而已。（停顿良久。）那么，一般了解的是，你的确有个自我，导向外在的活动，而以那种说法，你也有个内我。它也是有意识的，并且是所有自动的内在活动的指挥（加强语气地）。", "en": "In the first place, it is really impossible to separate portions of the self, and we make such distinctions only in an effort to explain the many facets of the personality. (Long pause.) It is generally understood, then, that you do have an ego, directed toward exterior activity, and in those terms (underlined) you also have an inner ego. It is also conscious, and is the director of all automatic interior activity (emphatically).", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0152", "zh": "大多数人不了解，他们的确有通路可以达到这内在的觉知。这内在自我或内在自己不该被认为比你的凡心（ordinary mind）优越。其实，它不该被认为是某个与你的凡心分开的东西。你的自我与你的平常意识将你所有的物质经验带入焦点，而使物质经验之出色的精确性成为可能。", "en": "Most people do not realize that they can indeed have access to this inner awareness. This inner ego or inner self should not be thought of as superior to your ordinary mind. It should not be thought of, really, as something separate from your ordinary mind. Your ego and your ordinary consciousness bring into focus all of your physical experiences, and make possible the brilliant preciseness of physical experience.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0154", "zh": "不过，内在自己却永远与其源头身份认同，自视为宇宙的一个被挚爱的、个别化的部分。它对是其传承的宇宙大爱是觉察的。", "en": "The inner ego, however, always identifies with its source-identity as a beloved, individualized portion of the universe. It is aware of the universal love that is its heritage.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "它天天在忙什么：你的身体和你的事件都是它做的", "note": "AI总结：外在自我忙着生存和操控物质世界，而世界能持续存在，靠的是内我不间断的警觉决定。它从里面指挥肉体的一切：作为潜意识的组织指挥者，它不只指挥身体的动作，也指挥那些没有它肉体就无法存在的存活机制；它知道何时启用安全阀，在外在自我惊觉之前就已觉察到危险。连物质本身都出自它的手：内在自我是把你这个层面能量投射进来的投射者，是你的对等物，它把能量拆解成简单成分，形成组成个体的分子和原子；它把知识放进浓缩形式，透过精神基因系统传给染色体系统，再转译成细胞遵循的物质密码；是它连同内在生命力和所有细胞的合作，才让身体作为一个独立结构存在、并维持本体感——没有内在自我的决心，本体的凝聚根本不可能。放到后期课的词汇里：是内我组织、发动、投射、掌控电磁能量单位，把能量变成物体、变成物质。事件也一样：你意识到的自我无法替你长骨头，推理再好也不能给自己压送血液；你想换工作时，内在事件会由内我安排，那涉及所有相关内我的沟通网；你可能不知不觉生了一场病又好了，是因为在架构二里内我既知道生病的理由也知道疗法，把补救的情境精确地安排到位。", "src": "第 50、51、55、119、509、822 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 50 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 51 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 55 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 119 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 509 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 822 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-008-e0003", "zh": "其实，全我一直不断经验所有内在感官传来的资料。内在自我当然觉察到这一点。潜意识有时觉察到这一点，而外在自我觉察到的非常少。其中的原因，我在过去的课程已经解释过了。外在自我必须将其大部分能量集中用于生存和操控外在的伪装世界。这个世界是由内我创造的，它的持续存在则是由于内我持续不断的警觉决定。", "en": "The fact is that the whole self is constantly experiencing data from all of the inner senses. The inner ego is of course aware of this. The subconscious is sometimes aware of this, and the outer ego is aware of very little. I have explained the reasons for this in past sessions. The outer ego must concentrate much of its energy toward survival in and manipulation of the outer camouflage world. This world has already been created by the inner self, and its continuing existence is determined by the constant vigilance of the inner self.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0024", "zh": "你将会明白，我们谈过很多次的内在自我，是把能量投射到你们层面的投射者。代表基本人格的内在自我，透过扩散让它自己化为物质，进入你们的层面。", "en": "Now, you will see that the inner ego of which we have spoken many times is the projector of energy upon your plane. The inner ego, representing the basic personality, through diffusion makes a materialization of itself and enters your plane.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第50节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "50", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0025", "zh": "所以内在自我是你们的对等物（counterpart）。它把能量拆解成简单的成分，但它仍然得在内在宇宙既有的法则之内运作。于是它形成将构成个体的个别分子和原子。它本身的知识被放进浓缩的形式之中，分子因此能够依据你们宇宙固有的物质特性结合与再结合。", "en": "The inner ego therefore is your counterpart. It breaks energy down into simple components, but it must still operate within the given laws of the inner universe. It therefore forms the separate molecules and atoms that will compose the individual. Its own knowledge is put into condensed form, and the molecules are therefore able to combine and recombine, according to the material properties inherent in your universe.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第50节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "50", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0027", "zh": "内我知道它的内容。这份内在资料，被当作整体分子意识，透过精神基因系统传递给染色体系统，然后，染色体系统再把资料转译成细胞遵循的物质密码。你会发现这与我们上一节的资料是相符的。", "en": "The inner ego knows what it is about. This inner data is transmitted through the mental genetic system by way of the generalized molecular consciousness to the chromosome system, and the chromosome system then translates data into a physical code for the cells to follow. You will find this fits in with the material from our previous session.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0032", "zh": "把它们的心灵完形转化为一个特定人类物质结构的细胞与分子，是从你们可称为外在环境之处分离出来的，但是它们与外在环境的连结程度却大过它们与外在环境的分离程度。是内在自我、内在生命力以及内在自我的决心，在构成肉体的所有细胞合作之下，才让人体这样一个特定的结构能够以分离的独立建构状态存在，并维持必要的本体感。", "en": "The cells and molecules, forming their psychic gestalt into a particular human physical structure, are separated from what you might call the outer environment, and yet they are also connected to the outer environment more than they are separated from it. It is the inner ego, and the inner vitality and the inner ego’s determination, along with the cooperation of all the cells that compose the physical body, that enables such a particular structure as the human body to exist as a separate construction, and to maintain the necessary sense of identity.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0033", "zh": "没有内在自我的决心，本体的凝聚是不可能的。你们所知的自己是很多东西，包含的厅室之多远超过你们现在的想像。甚至外在自我也包含无数个你们没有察觉的房间和交互连结。", "en": "Without the determination of the inner ego, cohesion of identity would be impossible. The self as you know it is many things, and contains many more vestibules and rooms than you now imagine. Even the outer ego contains multitudinous chambers and interconnections of which you are unaware.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0053", "zh": "在潜意识所有个人化的面向背后是自我或者说指挥意识；（directive consciousness）；不过是以休眠的方式，而且和荣格的论点相反的是，在潜意识之内以及在它那些个人化的面向之中，会发现过去转世的自己残余的记忆人格。它们可以被称为阴影，但它们并不是没有力量的。内在自我，潜意识的组织指挥者，也是自己的一部分，熟悉外在自我一无所知的活动和方法。这个组织者不仅从里面指挥肉体的活动，也从外面指挥那些个人的存活机制，没有那些机制，肉体无法存在，而且外在自我的存在也非常依赖它们。", "en": "It is the ego or directive consciousness behind all personified aspects of the subconscious; in dormant fashion however, and contrary to Jung’s propositions, within the subconscious and in those personified aspects of it will be found remnant memory personalities of past reincarnated selves. They may be called shadows and yet they are not powerless. The inner ego, the directive organizer of the subconscious, also is the part of the self which is familiar with activities and methods of which the outer ego is ignorant. It is this organizer who directs not only the movements of the physical body from within, but directs from within those intimate survival mechanisms, without which the physical body could not exist, and upon which the existence of the outer ego is so dependent.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0058", "zh": "内在自我知道何时运用安全阀，也会在外在自我注意到之前觉察到危险。内在自我和维护全我的基础与平衡有关，这非常重要，而乐于听取来自整体存有的讯息。内在自我透过内在感官接收讯息，对于外在自我因为它的专门化而无能认出的种种实相是有觉察的。在某些重要的面向上，外在自我本来某种程度代表依然居住在潜意识里的第二支配人格（subdominant personalities）。当外在自我狭隘，不足以代表这些第二支配人格时，它们就会揭竿而起，并趁状况有利之际，企图透过支配自我那一边暂时的软弱，来表达它们自己。但即使不这样做，它们也可以趁外在自我有幸浑然不觉时暂时接管，或透过单一功能，像是说话或动作，来表达它们自己。", "en": "The inner ego knows when to apply safety valves, and is aware of the danger before the outer ego is alerted. The inner ego is concerned with maintaining the foundations and balance, which is very important, of the whole self, and it is open to messages from the overall entity. The inner ego receives messages through the inner senses, and is aware of realities which the outer ego cannot afford to recognize because of its specialization. In some important aspects the outer ego is supposed to represent to some degree the subdominant personalities who still dwell in the subconscious. When the outer ego is narrow, and poorly represents these subdominant personalities then they rise up in arms, and when conditions are favorable attempt to express themselves through a momentary weakness on the part of the dominant ego. But without even doing this they may momentarily take over or express themselves through a single function, such as speech or motion, while the outer ego is blissfully unaware.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0124", "zh": "正是这个内我，以其浩瀚的知识与无限的意识范围，形成物理世界，并提供种种刺激，使自我不停地做着觉知的功课。正是这个内我——此处称为内自我——组织、发动、投射、掌控我们近来一直在谈的电磁能量单位，把能量转成物体，转成物质。", "en": "It is this inner self, out of the massive knowledge and unlimited scope of its consciousness, that forms the physical world, that provides stimuli to keep the ego constantly at the job of awareness . It is the inner self, termed here the inner ego, that organizes, initiates, projects, controls the EE units of which we have been speaking lately, transforming energy into objects, into matter.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0136", "zh": "举例而言，内我是觉察你转世活动的你自己的那部分。它是你那存在于时间之外，却又同时活在时间之内的部分。你形成你自己的实相。不过，你所觉察到的自我，显然无法为你形成你的身体或长你的骨头。但它知道如何估量世界的状况，它能演绎。你的推理能力是极为重要的，但单靠它却不能压送出你的血液，或告诉你的眼睛如何看。", "en": "The inner ego is a portion of the self, for example — is the portion of your self — that is aware of your reincarnational activities. It is the part of you that exists outside of time, yet simultaneously lives in time. You form your own reality. The ego that you are aware of obviously could not form your body for you, however, or grow your bones. It knows how to assess the conditions of the world. It makes deductions. Your reasoning is highly important, yet alone it cannot pump your blood or tell your eyes how to see.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0138", "zh": "如果你想改变工作，而心怀那个欲望，一个新的工作就会以完全同样的方式进入你的经验，因为内在事件会由内我来安排。一件身体上的事件涉及了许多肌肉关节等等的作用。就如涉及工作改变的一个事件也关系到许多人的动作，并且暗示了所有牵涉到的内我的一个沟通网。那么，显然的，一个具体的群体事件暗示了一种在比例上会把你们科技性沟通比下去的内在沟通系统。", "en": "If you want to change your job, and hold that desire, a new job will come into your experience in precisely the same fashion, in that the inner events will be arranged by the inner ego. A body event involves the working of numerous muscles and joints and so forth. An event involving a job change concerns motion on the part of many people, and implies a network of communication on the part of all of the inner egos involved. Obviously, then, a mass physical event implies an inner system of communications of proportions that would put your technological communications to shame.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0139", "zh": "口授：那么，再一次的，你可能不知不觉的染上一种病又恢复了，却从来没有觉察过你的毛病，而你被治愈是因为一连串似乎与那病本身毫无关系的事件——因为在“架构二”里内我知道患病及其痊愈的理由，带来会弥补那状况的那些适当的情境。当没有事阻碍了复原的时候，这种事情就会自动的发生。 在内在与外在自我之间的沟通显然应该尽可能的清晰而开放。一般而言，内我依靠你对具体事件的估量。你对你生活隐私面的关注以及你在群体事件中的参与，都与你对具体情况的估量以及你对它的信念与欲望极有关系。", "en": "Dictation: You may then, again, unknowingly acquire an illness and recover, never aware of your malady, being healed because of a series of events that would seemingly have nothing to do with the illness itself — because in Framework 2 the inner ego, knowing both the reason for the illness, and its cure, brought about those precise situations that remedied the condition. Such events happen automatically, when nothing hampers recovery at your end.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "外在自我只是前台：两个「我」的关系", "note": "AI总结：赛斯说得很不客气：内在自我非常了解外在自我，而外在自我只是内在自我的假象——但内我知道你走的每一步、你呼吸的每一口空气、你做的每一个梦；当你领悟到你远比那个自我本位的「我是」大多了，就不再为摸不到内里而烦恼。关系是颠倒的：内在自我一直是潜意识的中心，外向意识的中心——那个外在自我——反而是内我在某些部分展现更强的客观化倾向后挑出来的发言人。两个人格面向各有辖区：外我是人格与物质环境打交道时善于组织的面向，内在自我则是与内在环境打交道时的另一个组织面貌；两者一同运作——一个让你在已知的世界里操纵自如，一个带给你那些没有它肉体生活就无法维持的微妙内在知觉；一个向内看、向发端的冲动冲刺，一个向外推。麻烦出在内与外闹翻的时候：当内在自我与外在自我追求完全相反的观点与目标，全我就被大大拒于价值完成之外——历史上这样的分割发生过好几次，现在也在发生。外我还不愿认账：它不想见到内在自我，不想承认它存在——就像眼睛没有镜子看不到自己的瞳孔，要不是内我藏在所有倒影深处，外我连自己都看不到；外我看物质世界时，照见的其实是自己内我的脸。对心理学家，赛斯只补一句：荣格说得对的部分是自我无法直接认识无意识材料，但他不知道有一个内我，正是它组织着所谓无意识的经验，创造出外我随后才去打交道的那重物理实相。外我不是提线木偶，只是意识较少、感知较少、远不那么稳定——尽管它煞有介事地假装稳定。", "src": "第 37、50、58、119、151、165、283、509、512 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 37 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 50 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 119 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 165 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 283 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 509 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-008-e0016", "zh": "内在自我非常了解外在自我。外在自我只是内在自我的假象。外在自我通常不能觉察，当下你们可能把什么东西当成内在自我的思想或讯息；但是内在自我知道你们采取的每一个步骤、你呼吸空气的每一个分子，你做的每一个梦；而且它是你自己人格的源头，并代表你人格所属的存有部分。", "en": "This inner ego knows the outer ego well. The outer ego is but a counterfeit image of the inner ego. The outer ego as a rule is not aware of what you may think of for now as the thoughts or communications of the inner ego; but the inner ego knows every step you take, every particle of air you breathe, every dream you have; and it is the source of your own personality and is the representative of the entity of which it is part.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0023", "zh": "当你们了悟到你们远比自我本位的“我是”大多了，也明白你们真正的人格包含一个更大、更有力量的内我时，这种外在自我相对无法取得那份知识的状况，将不会再困扰你们。", "en": "When you realize that you are much more than the egotistical “I am,” and that your true personality contains a much larger and really more powerful inner ego, then this relative inavailability of inner comprehension to the outer ego will not annoy you.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第50节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "50", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0040", "zh": "当内在自我与外在自我追求完全相反的观点以及不同的目标和目的时，你们就遇到困难了。在研究人类的人格和心灵上，你们的心理学家走得不远，也不够深。当一道全面，或接近全面的障碍存在内在自我与外在自我之间时，全我就会很大程度被拒于价值完成之外。这样的分割曾在历史上发生过好几次，目前也正在发生。", "en": "When the inner ego and the outer ego pursue directly opposed viewpoints and different aims and goals, then you run into difficulty. In studying human personality and the psyche, your psychologists have not gone far, nor deeply enough. When a complete barrier, or nearly complete barrier, exists between the inner and outer egos, then the whole self is denied value fulfillment to a large degree. Such a division occurs at various times in history, and is occurring now.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0054", "zh": "在很多方面，它是一个反映者，自己那往外看的表面。虽然这是必要的，但自己整个剩下来的部分不能留给一个没有把注意力集中在深处之内，而是坐在房子的前廊，丢着内在工作不管的组织者或照顾者。外在自我不想要见到内在自我。外在自我不想要承认内在自我的存在。就像没有镜子，眼睛看不到它自己的瞳孔，同样的，要不是内在自我藏在所有倒影的深处，外在自我连它自己都看不到。", "en": "In many respects it is a reflector, the surface of the self looking outward. While this is necessary, the whole remainder of the self could not be left to an organizer or caretaker who did not focus his attentions within the depths but sat, as it were, on the front porch of the house, leaving the inner workings unattended. The outer ego does not want to meet the inner ego. The outer ego does not want to admit the existence of the inner ego. As the eye cannot see its own pupil without a mirror, so the outer ego could not even see itself, were it not that the inner ego hides in the depths of all reflections.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0055", "zh": "当外在自我，从它意识的表面，反映外在世界时，它看见内在自我的倒影，它们是在它自己眼睛之内的影像；就像自己在它自己的眼睛之内潜意识地创造物质，就像自己在潜意识里而不是在意识里创造物质，就像自己按照内在而不是外在的预期创造物质，同样的，自我也是，在观看物质宇宙时，与它自己内在自我的脸打照面；外在自我无法逃离这个内我。", "en": "When the outer ego, from the surface of its consciousness, reflects the outer world, it sees reflections of the inner ego which are the images within its own eye; and as the self creates matter subconsciously within its own eye, and as the self creates matter subconsciously and not consciously, and as the self creates matter in line with inner and not outer expectations, so then does the ego, in viewing the material universe, come face to face with the face of its own inner ego; and the outer ego cannot escape from this inner self.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0059", "zh": "意识在潜意识里有它的根源，它从中跃出。意识并非曾经位于潜意识的中心。但是，内在自我一直都是潜意识的中心。", "en": "The consciousness had its origin in the subconscious, from which it sprang. The consciousness was not at one time the center of the subconscious. However, the inner ego was always the center of the subconscious.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0060", "zh": "意识的中心，也就是外向意识（outward consciousness）的中心，外在自我，在内我的某些部分展现更大的客观化倾向之后，最终被内在自我选上；这些部分当然绕着潜意识次人格的其中之一集结，然后胜出，成为外在自我，担任全我的操纵者和发言人。", "en": "The center of consciousness, that is the center of outward consciousness, the outer ego, is finally chosen by the inner ego after certain portions of the inner self show greater tendencies for objectification; these portions of course grouped around one of the subconscious subpersonalities which then wins out to become the outer ego, the manipulator for and the spokesman for the whole self.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0063", "zh": "只有一些细微的差别与不同，就这样而已。内在自我是内我当中与外在自我紧密连结的那一部分，因为它某个程度是功能和活动的指导者。但它并没有精确地聚焦，它向内看。这里我们碰到语言方面的难题。", "en": "There are shadings and variations and that is all. The inner ego is that part of the inner self which is closely allied with the outer ego, in that it is to some degree a director of function and activity. But it is not sharply focused. It looks inward. Here we run into some language difficulty.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0079", "zh": "习惯性接受某几类行动，或习惯性拒绝某几类行动，都可以视为自我的特点。不过，自我并不是人格中唯一善于组织的面向，它只是人格与物质环境打交道时，善于组织的那个面向而已。内在自我则是人格与内在环境打交道时，善于组织的另一个面貌。", "en": "The ego, then, is as much characterized by those types of action which it habitually denies, as by those types of actions which it habitually accepts. It is not the only organizing aspect of the personality, however. It is simply the organizing aspect of the personality in its dealings with the physical environment. The inner ego is another organizing feature of the personality in its dealings with inner environment.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第165节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "165", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0122", "zh": "他有一点说得很好：自我无法直接认识无意识材料。然而，他并没有意识到——你们的心理学家也并没有——我告诉过你们很多次的事：有一个内自我；正是这个内自我，在组织荣格所谓的无意识材料。", "en": "He makes a good point, saying that the ego cannot know unconscious material directly. He does not realize however, nor do your other psychologists, what I have told you often —that there is an inner ego; and it is this inner ego that organizes what Jung would call unconscious material.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0123", "zh": "内自我正是那些荣格会称为无意识的经验的组织者。内自我是我们所称的内我的另一个名称。外我在环境与物理实相之中操纵运作，内自我、或者说内我，便在内在的实相之中组织与操纵。内自我创造出那重物理实相，外我随后才与之打交道。", "en": "Now the inner ego is the organizer of experience that Jung would call unconscious. The inner ego is another term for what we call the inner self. As the outer ego manipulates within the environment and physical reality, so the inner ego or self organizes and manipulates within an inner reality. The inner ego creates that physical reality with which the outer ego then deals.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0125", "zh": "这并不是说外我是个提线木偶。这只是说：外我的意识远少于内自我、少于内我；它的感知较少；它也远不那么稳定——尽管它煞有介事地假装稳定；它是从内我涌出的，它的觉知是更少，而不是更多。（停顿。）", "en": "This is not to say that the outer ego is a puppet. It is to say that the outer ego is far less conscious than the inner ego or the inner self, that its perception is less, that it is far less stable, though it makes great pretense at stability; that it springs from the inner self, and is less rather than more, aware. (Pause.)", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0128", "zh": "“外在自我”与内在自我一同运作，其一，让你能在你所知的世界里操纵自如，另一，带给你那些微妙的内在知觉，没有它们，肉体生活即不可能维持。", "en": "The “outer ego” and the inner ego operate together, the one to enable you to manipulate in the world that you know, the other to bring you those delicate inner perceptions without which physical existence could not be maintained.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "在哪能见到它：梦里、出神里、灵感来的时候", "note": "AI总结：最日常的入口是梦：内在自我其实就是那个做梦的自己，是自我的「我」睡觉时体验的那个「我」，是梦里的「我」；它也是灵体的「我」。它不只是做梦，还当编辑——梦人格找到的解决办法会被它自动捡起来，传送给各个层面的自己；梦境处理来自两个架构的事件，你用信念与意图告诉内我，在无量的可能事件里你想遇上哪一个；梦还是一种转译，架构二的事件在梦里以象征形式出现。往深处走是融合：当内在自我与外在自我融合到某种程度，代表一种新意识的形成——把醒时的「我」带进梦状态是条路，醒时状态也可能开启门户；一旦发生，直觉泉源会冲到表面，外我照常履职，却知道还有更多东西牵涉在内。罗自己的梦就被赛斯点名：后窗看到自己那次正是两个自我的融合，吓到的外我把一场绝佳的投射拦了下来。日常版本是：内我会把自己安插进醒时意识里，可能带来短暂的方向迷失；灵感就是从内在自我接收来的。实操要点有两条：外我可以调整自己、配合内我，用内在而非外在感官聚焦能量，直接体验内在实相；同时要给必要的内在自我质疑对话留出时间——把信心全交给外在权威的人，恰恰是没留这个时间。", "src": "第 58、88、173、202、283、663、823 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 88 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 173 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 202 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 283 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 663 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 823 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-008-e0039", "zh": "就自己与非自己来说，你们知道，自己这个单位是由主导整个能量场的内在自我组织起来的。外在自我指挥这个完形在物质宇宙中的操纵。外在自我与物质属性的关系更紧密，而且它能够透过调整自己配合内我而改变焦点，用内在而非外在感官来聚焦能量，而直接体验内在实相。这是目前为止最有利的内在实相体验方法，因为外在自我因此能够有意识地觉察事情的来龙去脉，也能够在它自己的范畴中利用这种知识。", "en": "As far as self and not-self are concerned, the unit of self is organized, as you know, by the inner ego, which directs the whole energy field. The outer ego directs the manipulation of this gestalt in the physical universe. The outer ego is rather more tied to physical properties, and yet it can directly experience inner reality by a change of focus through aligning itself with the inner ego, focusing its energies with the inner rather than the outer senses. This is by far the most advantageous method of experiencing inner reality, because the outer ego is therefore consciously aware of what has been going on, and can use such knowledge in its own sphere.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0048", "zh": "自我无法这样改变它的焦点，但我们谈过的内在自我，其实就是那个做梦的自己，也是当自我的“我”睡觉时体验的那个“我”。", "en": "The ego cannot so change its focus, but the inner ego of which we have spoken is indeed the self that dreams, and is the “I” who experiences when the ego “I” sleeps.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第88节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "88", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0081", "zh": "实际上，内在自我就是你们梦里面的“我”，它在内我里面的位置就跟自我在物质的自己（physical self）当中的位置有点类似。不过，行动会融入内在自我当中，觉知的范围更复杂。我们后面会讨论这个内在自我跟梦境和健康之间的关联。", "en": "The inner ego is indeed the “I” of your dreams, having somewhat the same sort of position within the inner self as the ego itself has to the physical self. Actions however merge within the inner ego. The scope of awareness is more complex. We will at a later time discuss this inner ego in connection with the dream situation and health.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第173节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "173", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0082", "zh": "不过，内在自我多少也了解它们的活动。内在自我会自动捡拾这些梦中人格找到的解决方法，并传送给各个不同层面的自己。人格如果改变，梦世界就会改变，因为梦世界永远都是流动多变的人格架构其中的一部分。", "en": "The inner ego however is to some degree still familiar with their activities. Solutions found by these dream personalities are automatically picked up by the inner ego, and transmitted to the various levels of the self. The dream world changes as the personality changes, so that it is always a part of the mobile personality framework.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第173节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "173", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0089", "zh": "内在自我就是灵体（astral body）的“我”。", "en": "The inner ego is then the “I” of the astral body.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第202节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "202", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0109", "zh": "当然，它某种程度上必定是成功的，不然你所知的物质导向人格就不存在了。自我当然是行动的一部分。然而，行动有无穷无尽的层面是自我感知不到的。内在自我和外在自我是可能融合到某种程度，而且这种融合在发生时的确代表一种新意识的形成。", "en": "It must, of course, succeed to some extent, or the physically oriented personality as you know it would not exist. The ego is of course a part of action. There are endless levels of action however, which the ego does not perceive. It is possible for the inner and outer egos to merge to some extent, and this merging when it occurs does indeed represent the formation of a new kind of consciousness.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0110", "zh": "这个观念算不上是新观念。它不是一般公认的理论，但它却源远流长。当你带着醒时的我(waking I）进入梦状态，这就是通往此一不同意识的途经。还有一个门户可能出现在醒时状况中。当这个门户开启时，内在自我和外在自我就会融合。外在自我认得它自己的职责，但它也觉察到还有更多东西牵涉在内。", "en": "This concept is hardly a new one. It is not a generally accepted theory, but it has ancient roots. When you carry the waking I into the dream state, this is one approach to this different consciousness. There is also an opening up that can occur in the waking condition. When this occurs the inner and outer egos merge. The outer ego recognizes its own duties, but it is aware that more is involved.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0111", "zh": "外在自我感应到它通常不得其门而入的实相。它想：“还有更多，但是我无法跟过去。”这里，有了这个了悟之后，内在自我可能会突然开启。直觉泉源冲到表面，因为外在自我已经改变了，它能够接受这些实相，同时依然履行它平常的职责。", "en": "It senses realities usually closed to it. It thinks, “There is more, but beyond I cannot follow.” Here with this realization the inner ego may suddenly open. Intuitive springs rush to the surface, and because the outer ego has already been alerted, it is able to accept these realities while still performing its ordinary duties.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0112", "zh": "需要的发展很多都发生在梦状态中。约瑟，我想要提一下你在你家的后窗看到你自己的那一个梦。内在自我和外在自我融合了。受到惊吓的外在自我确实拦住你，不让你有一次绝佳的投射。", "en": "Much of the needed development takes place in the dream state. I wanted to mention that particular dream of yours, Joseph, in which you saw yourself at your back window. There was a merging of inner and outer egos. The startled outer ego did indeed hold you back from an excellent projection.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0113", "zh": "它是有觉知也有意识的。然而，它只是因为发现身体好像处于一个平常不可能的位置，所以吓到了。下一次，它会改进。不过，同样的，你们两人也会发现内在自我把它自己安插在醒时意识期间，而且可能会或可能不会暂时迷失方向。", "en": "It was aware, and conscious. However it was simply frightened to find what seemed like the body in a position normally impossible for it. The next time it will go further. In the same way however you will both find the inner ego inserting itself into periods of waking consciousness, and there may or may not be a momentary disorientation.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0131", "zh": "个人的信心愈来愈被转移到一个外在力量上。这通常表示，没有给必要的内在自我质疑对话所需的时间；本来可以发生的自我疗愈，却由对另一个人的信心带来，然而，它的效力并不能维持很久。", "en": "The individual’s faith is transferred more and more to an outside agency. This usually means that no time is allowed for necessary inner dialogues of self questioning, and the self-healing that might otherwise occur is brought about through belief in another. This can only go on for so long, however.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第663节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "663", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0143", "zh": "我说内我会推理，但其推理并不受限于因与果之限制。内我在“架构二”的较广范围内之行动，解释了许多在你们世界里本来仿佛不合理的事件及看起来的巧合。在“架构二”之内的许多实相，无法适当的在“架构一”里向你解释为事实，只因为它们涉及了无法被转译为如你所认为的事实之心理厚度。反之，这些常常以艺术的象征语言出现，而你们许多的梦都是一种转译，在其中，“架构二”的事件以象征形式出现。", "en": "I said that the inner ego reasons, but its reasoning is not restricted to the cause-and-effect limitations that you apply to the reasoning process. The action of the inner ego within the wider sphere of Framework 2 explains many events and seeming coincidences that otherwise seem to make no sense within your world. Many realities within Framework 2 cannot suitably be explained as facts to you in Framework 1, simply because they involve psychological thicknesses that cannot be translated into facts as you think of them. These often appear in the symbolic language of the arts instead, and many of your dreams are translations in which the events of Framework 2 appear in symbolic form.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第823节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "823", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0145", "zh": "你们每一个人以信念与意图告诉内我，在无量的可能事件中你想遇上哪一个。在梦境，由两个架构来的事件都被处理。梦境不只牵涉到存在于两个实相架构之间的一种意识状态，却还牵涉到——以那种说法——一个连接的实相本身。在此，我想强调所有种类的植物与动物生命都“做梦”。这同样适用于原子分子及任何“粒子”的“心理活动”。", "en": "[Each of] you, with your beliefs and intents, tell the inner ego which of an infinite number of probable events you want to encounter. In the dream state events from both frameworks are processed. The dream state involves not only a state of consciousness that exists between the two frameworks of reality, but also involves, in those terms, a connecting reality of its own. Here I would like to emphasize that to one degree or another all species of plant and animal life “dream.” The same applies to the “psychological activity” of atoms and molecules, and any “particle.”2 Period.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第823节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "823", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "它的时间：广阔的现在，和被感知的「未来」", "note": "AI总结：内在自我不受钟表时间束缚——钟表时间是伪装，没有障碍就没有时间，它觉察到的障碍少，被时间绑的程度就低。它活在广阔的现在里，那是全我存在的基本时间。所以那些让人发毛的说法其实是平实描述：内在自我知道外在自我将用自由意志做出的任何选择——不是决定论，而是未来对它而言并不存在，它自然能看到外我看不到的地方；你从第一页开始读资料，不代表第400页还不存在，外我被逼进连续的行动里，内我没有这种束缚。它还是可能性的经手人：一个人面对三种行动选了一种在物质场域经验，另外两种也被经验了，其结果由内在自我感知；它看见整个本体同时存在于不同维度之中，而外我企图把行动截短，只看得见生与死。它持续运作却永远处于变为的状态，包含现有人格的全部潜力的心理蓝图；它是所有活动——醒时与梦中——的指挥者，是整个现有人格的主要本体，肉体存在之后存活下来的那个「我」。", "src": "第 36、226、231、232、270、290 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 36 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 226 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 231 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 232 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 270 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 290 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-008-e0008", "zh": "很真实的是，内在自我透过内在感官觉察任何的选择，而外在自我则使用自由意志做出选择。这并不是说，各个决定不管怎样都是事先决定的。而只是说，内在自我不受自由意志在做选择的那个维度束缚。", "en": "It is quite true that the inner ego is aware through the inner senses of any choices that the outer ego will make with the use of free will. This does not mean that decisions are in any way predetermined. It only means that the inner ego is not bound by the dimensions in which those free will choices are made.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0009", "zh": "你们知道，你们的钟表时间是伪装，对内在自我而言，钟表时间并不存在。这一点你们的确不应该觉得奇怪，因为你们知道，你们现在的人格甚至可以通过使用心理时间，而在一定程度上逃离钟表时间。我曾经说过，没有障碍，就没有时间。内在自我意识到的障碍很少，因此被时间束缚的程度不像外在自我那么大。", "en": "Your clock time as you know is camouflage, and does not exist as far as the inner ego is concerned. This certainly should not be strange to you, since you know that even your present personalities can to some extent escape from clock time through the use of psychological time. I have said that there is no time without barriers. The inner ego is aware of fewer barriers and therefore is not bound by time to the degree that the outer ego is bound.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0011", "zh": "为了业的理由，人格被他们自己的存有设定了很多的限制。我想清楚说明一下，自由意志的确存在，但存有这边透过使用更大的自由意志，而限制了它。此外，内在自我觉知所谓的未来决定，那并不是因为它把这样的决定强加到外在自我之上，而完全是因为像这样的未来，对内在自我来说并不存在，因此它可以感知到外在自我感知不到的地方。", "en": "Many limitations are set upon personalities by their own entities for karmic reasons. I want to make it plain that free will does exist, but that it is limited through use of a more extended free will on the part of the entity. Also, the inner ego is aware of so-called future decisions not because he forces such decisions upon the outer ego but simply because the future as such does not exist to the inner ego, and therefore he can perceive where the outer ego cannot.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0012", "zh": "举例来说，一个人开始看这份资料的第一页，这并不是意味着第400页还没存在。你们的外在自我被迫进入可称为连续的行动之中，但内在自我就没有受到这种束缚。这应该澄清这个重点了。我之前提过，因果以不同的方式在运作，看起来象是因和果的关系，通常只是你们必须用连续的方式看待行动而产生的结果。", "en": "Although someone begins reading this material on page one, for example, this does not mean that page four hundred does not already exist. Your outer ego is forced into what could be called successive action, but the inner ego is not so bound. This should make the point more clear. I mentioned earlier that cause and effect operates in various manners, and what seems to be cause and effect is often merely a result of your necessary disposition to view actions in a successive manner.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0094", "zh": "——随着内在自我有意识地运作来给予连续性。", "en": "—with the inner ego operating consciously to give continuity.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第226节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "226", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0097", "zh": "就如你所知道的，内在自我存在的时间是广阔的现在。广阔的现在是全我存在的基本时间，但自己的不同部分经验着它们自己的时间系统，那是它们感知的独有方式的结果。", "en": "Now, the time in which the inner ego exists is, as you know, the spacious present. The spacious present is the basic time in which the whole self has its existence, but the various portions of that self have their experience in their own time systems, which are the results of their characteristic methods of perception.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第231节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "231", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0098", "zh": "让我们思考一下下面的内容。在你们系统里的一个人——这是非常简化的说法——这个人发现他有三种行动的选择。他选择其中的一种，并且在物质的场域里经验它。不过其他两种行动也被经验了，但不是在物质的系统。其他两种行动的结果被内在自我所感知。", "en": "Let us consider the following. The individual within your system—and this is quite simplified—an individual finds himself with a choice of three actions. He chooses one of these and experiences it within the physical field. The other two actions are experienced however, but not within the physical system. The results of the other two actions are perceived by the inner ego.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第232节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "232", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0102", "zh": "在这样的梦中，你的感知似乎清晰至极，你可以确定内在自我正在运作。现在，人格，现有人格的所有部分，都属于这个内在自我。它持续不断运转，但始终处于变为的状态。它不只是你在你们的时间当中任何既定时刻的你所是而已。它包含而且就是心理蓝图，现有人格在任何既定的转世之内的全部潜力就包含在这个蓝图之中。", "en": "When in such dreams your perceptions seem exceedingly clear, you can be certain that the inner ego is operating. Now all portions of the personality, of the present personality, belong to this inner ego. It functions constantly, and yet it is always in a state of becoming. It is more than what you are at any given moment in your time. It contains, and j^, the psychological blueprint containing the full potential of the present personality within any given incarnation.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第270节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "270", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0103", "zh": "因此，无论是在醒时还是在梦中，它都是所有活动的指挥者。你的灵感就是从内在自我接收来的，而同意我们聚会的也是内在自我。", "en": "It is therefore the director of afi activities, both in the waking and dream condition. It is the inner ego from whom you receive your inspiration, and it is the inner ego which gives consent to our meetings.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第270节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "270", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0105", "zh": "内在自我是整个现有人格的主要本体。在很多情况下，它是你梦里的那个“我”（I）。它绝对是你的创造活动里的那个我。你看，在物质存在之后存活下来的是那个我，而物质导向的自我只是它的一部分而已。", "en": "It is the prime identity of the whole present personality. In many cases it is the I of your dreams. It is definitely the I of your creative activity. It is the I, you see, which survives physical existence, and the physical, physically-oriented ego is only a part of it.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第270节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "270", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0115", "zh": "内在自我看见也知道它自己是这个行动或事件的一部分，而且它看见整个本体同时存在于各个不同的维度之中。外在自我企图缩短行动，所以它的观点受到它自己的企图限制。它感知它的出生和它的死亡，却没有超越它的出生和它的死亡。", "en": "The inner ego sees and knows itself as a part of this action or happening, and sees the entire identity existing in various dimensions simultaneously. The outer ego attempts to cut action short, and so its viewpoint is limited by its own attempt. It perceives its birth and its death, but not beyond its birth or its death.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第290节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "290", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "它也不是静止的：拆了又装、内变成外", "note": "AI总结：别把内在自我想成一个固定的高层官员。你其实每时每刻都被拆解百万次、再以各种方式组合，但你始终保有内我、保有本体——只是这个本体必须改变。本体的凝聚力从内在经由内在感官投射到物质结构上；每一个自己在最真实的意义上都是无限的，透过内在感官与那个不可见的内在宇宙亲密连结。它的来历也流动：有的外在自我选择成为自己的存有，那个了不起的外我进而变成一个内在自我，再从它未实现的欲望与能力形成新的外在自我；走向更深的内在，终究会带你走到另一个外在——外我会遇见内我，反之亦然。它向内聚焦的强度与外我向外聚焦一样，本身也是个复合体；所有这些划分都是武断的，界线只是注意力焦点的差别。最好的图像是：潜意识是个核心，被内在自我和外在自我包围，两边都充满创造力，只是焦点不同；自我、内在自我、潜意识、全我、存有，全都是张力状态，而沟通正是张力造成的结果。透过潜意识，内在自我会适时促进某些能力的发展，让全我更能达成平衡与实现；当自我经由训练变得更像内在自我，它会敞开，接收到先前被否定的内在经验。", "src": "第 54、55、58、59、153、309 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 54 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 55 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 59 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 153 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 309 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-008-e0028", "zh": "我建议你们休息（break）一下，如果这样还拆解（break）不了你们（译注：赛斯在此用break有休息与瓦解之意的双关语。），那就没办法了。你们其实像你们看到的那样被拆解百万次，再用各种不同的方式组合在一起；可是你保有内我，换句话说就是，你自己的本体。但是这个本体必须改变。这同样的没有任何矛盾之处。没有任何事物是静止不动的，而且信不信由你，没有任何事物。", "en": "I suggest your break, and if this hasn’t broken you up then nothing will. You are indeed as you can see broken up a million times, and put together in many various manners; and yet you retain the inner ego, and in other words your own identity. But this identity must change. This again is no contradiction. Nothing can be static, and believe it or not, nothing is.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0034", "zh": "这里的重点是，本体的凝聚力从内在，也就是说，从内在自我经由内在感官，被投射到人类的物质结构上。这当然也包括构成细胞的个别分子和原子与生俱来的意识。", "en": "The important point here is that identity cohesion is projected upon the human physical structure from within, that is, from the inner ego by way of the inner senses. This of course includes the consciousness also, that is inherent in the separate molecules and atoms that compose the cells.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0035", "zh": "自己的这些界限、限制、广度和前景都只是依据主观而定。就非常真实的意义而言，每一个自己都是无限的、没有束缚的，在你们层面以最亲密的方式与宇宙中的万物连结在一起；透过内在感官，内在自我也以最亲密的方式与未知的、不可见的内在宇宙连结在一起。", "en": "The boundaries, limitations, extent and vistas of the self are merely arbitrary. In a very true sense each self is infinite, unbounded, connected in a most intimate way to all other things in the universe on your plane; and through the inner senses and the inner ego connected also in a most intimate way to the unknown and unseen inner universe.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0042", "zh": "其他的自我反而选择成为它们自己的存有，在这种例子里，那了不起的自我进而变为一个内在自我，然后从它自己未实现的欲望、能力和行动，形成许多新的外在自我，再度寻求价值完成。", "en": "Other egos choose instead to become entities of their own, in which case this magnificent outer ego becomes in turn an inner ego, which then from its own unfulfilled desires, abilities and initiatives are formed new outer egos which once again seek fulfillment.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0044", "zh": "这里我们很可能会碰到一些困难，但我会设法解释我的意思，以后也会理清所有疑问。自己有一个内在自我和一个外在自我，同样的，内在最终也会变成外在。举例来说，理论上，如果贯彻到底的话，一个通往可以说内在更深处的深度出神，终究会带你走进另一个外在。比方说外在自我会遇到内在自我，反之亦然。", "en": "Here we will most probably run into some difficulty, but I will try to explain what I mean, and will clear up any questions later. As the self has an inner and an outer ego, so also does the inside finally become the outside. Theoretically for example, if followed through, a deep trance leading to a deeper inside so to speak, would bring you ultimately to another outside. The outer ego for example would meet the inner ego, and vice versa.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0066", "zh": "内在自我向内聚焦，强度和外在自我向外聚焦一样。这个内在自我，在很多方面，是一个复合体，和外在自我一样其实都是复合体，只不过后者程度较小。", "en": "The inner ego is focused inward, with as much intensity as the outer ego is focused outward. This inner ego is in many respects a composite, as indeed to a lesser degree the outer ego is a composite.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0067", "zh": "然而，内在自我，在意识到自己的同时，已回到行动之内的主观位置，把它自己看成是行动的一部分。而外在自我，如果你记得的话，则把它自己看成和行动分离。内在自我怀着各种目的，那是存有一直努力达成这些在它的各个人格身上可见的目的。", "en": "The inner ego, however, while conscious of itself, has returned to a subjective position within action, and views itself as a part of action. The outer ego, if you recall, views itself as apart from, or separate from, action. The inner ego contains the various purposes toward which the entity, as seen in its various personalities, has been working to achieve.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0069", "zh": "我经常说，所有这些区分或分隔都是武断的，全部都是一个存在于另一个之内。外显的界线不是界线，只是注意力的焦点有别而已。甚至这个内在自我从这一刻到另一刻都不是同一个，因为它不是一个静止的东西，而是连续行动的一部分。不过，内在自我对潜意识、梦宇宙和内我，远比外在自我熟悉多了。", "en": "I have often said that all these divisions and separations are arbitrary. All exist one within another. Apparent boundaries are not boundaries, but only differences in the focus of attention. Even this inner ego is not the same from one given moment to another, for it is not a static thing, but is a part of continuing action. It is much more familiar with the subconscious and with the dream universe, and with the inner self, than it is with the outside ego, however.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0070", "zh": "在某种程度上，它也表现得像是个经验与行动的指导者。它其实不是由过去的自我，而是由各个不同人格的那些支配面向组成。内在自我，本身也是行动，朝着一个往内的方向冲刺；也就是说，朝着发端的冲动回溯，外在自我则是往外面冲刺。所以说，它们是两张脸，形成很多行动领域之中的一个，一个往内拉，一个往外推。", "en": "To some extent it also acts like a director of experience and action. It is not actually composed of the past egos, but of those dominant aspects of the various personalities. The inner ego, as action, thrusts in an inward direction; that is, back toward the originating impulse. The outside ego thrusts outward. They are two faces, therefore, and form one of many spheres of action, one pulling inward and one outward.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0071", "zh": "外在自我一直充满创造力，内在自我也是。只是创造所在的焦点不同而已。可以想像潜意识是一个核心，被内在自我和外在自我包围。这里维持着某些张力，顺便提一下，所有的沟通都是张力造成的结果。", "en": "As the outer ego is constantly creative, so is the inner ego. The focus in which the creativity occurs is merely different. The subconscious could be thought of as a nucleus, surrounded by the inner and outer egos. Certain tensions are maintained here, and all communications, incidentally, are the results of tensions.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0072", "zh": "自我、内在自我、潜意识、全我、甚至存有，这些全都是张力状态。", "en": "The ego, the inner ego, the subconscious, the whole self, and even the entity, these are all states of tension.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0073", "zh": "不过，透过潜意识，内在自我有时候可能促进某些能力的发展，使全我更能够达成平衡和实现。", "en": "The inner ego, however, through the subconscious, may at times encourage the development of abilities that will better allow the whole self to achieve balance and fulfillment.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第153节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "153", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-008-e0117", "zh": "很多实际的物质干预步骤被删除了。相对来说，自我变得越来越像内在自我，而不是它旧有的自己。之前内在实相的众多部分曾被否定，但是现在这个改变的自我对它们是有觉知的。在结构上，它依然完整无缺，可是在化学和电磁上，它已经改变了。它有能力敞开了，这样才能够接收到内在经验。", "en": "Many actual physical intervening steps are cut out. The ego becomes more similar to the inner ego than to its old self, comparatively speaking. This altered ego is aware of large portions of inner reality that were previously denied. Structurally it remains intact, and yet it has changed chemically, and electromagnetically. It is able to open up so that inner experience can be received.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第309节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "309", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 13}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 11}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 8}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 4}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 3}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 2}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 1}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 6, "quotes": 75, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 16}};
